    21	loop: sidecar restarted first, overlapping ticks skipped with a warning, a "Run now"
    22	command on the dashboard, local time zone. Cronos (cron next-occurrence math) is this
    23	package's only dependency beyond Aspire itself.
    24	
    25	## Usage
    26	
    27	One entry point in the AppHost, two backends of the same discovered truth:
    28	
    29	```csharp
    30	using System.Reflection;
    31	using Intropy.Topology.Aspire;
    32	using Intropy.Topology.Generation;
    33	
    34	var assembly = Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly();
    35	return args is ["run", ..] or []
    36	    ? await IntropyAspire.RunAsync(assembly, args)     // → Aspire + DCP
    37	    : await IntropyGenerate.RunAsync(assembly, args);  // → generate | check | graph
    38	```
    39	
    40	Each component is resolved to the sibling project that runs it by folder convention
    41	(`order-extractor` → `../order-extractor/order-extractor.csproj`). A component can instead be mapped
    42	to a container image, and external systems can be mocked, via the `IDevProfile` seam on the system
    43	definition:
    44	
    45	```csharp
    46	public sealed class OrderFulfillmentSystem : ISystemDefinition, IDevProfile
    47	{
    48	    public string SystemName => "order-fulfillment";
    49	    public void Define(SystemBuilder builder) { /* ... topology ... */ }
    50	
    51	    public void ConfigureDev(DevBuilder dev)
    52	    {
    53	        dev.MockExternalSystem("webshop", "atmoz/sftp:latest", 2222);
    54	        dev.Override("erp-order-loader", "myregistry/erp-loader:1.0"); // run as a container, not a project
    55	
    56	        // Contract-backed mocks, served by one Microcks instance (docs/decisions/0006):
    57	        dev.MockHttpExternalSystem("erp", "mocks/erp-orders-openapi.yaml", "erp-orders", "1.0.0");
    58	        dev.MockApi("freight-booking", "mocks/freight-api-openapi.yaml", "freight-booking-api", "1.0.0");
    59	    }
    60	}
    61	```
    62	
    63	`MockHttpExternalSystem` points a `bindings.http` connector at a REST mock generated from the
    64	OpenAPI contract. `MockApi` mocks an *internal* API: its provider component is not started, and a
    65	generated Dapr `HTTPEndpoint` resource routes service invocation of the provider's app-id to the
    66	mock — so a single component can be debugged without running its siblings. Artifact paths resolve
    67	against the AppHost project directory; `serviceName`/`serviceVersion` must match the contract's
    68	`info.title`/`info.version`.
    69	
    70	Dev declarations never enter the `SystemTopology`, so the prod model stays pure.
    71	
    72	## Prerequisites for `run`
    73	
    74	- The [.NET Aspire](https://aspire.dev) tooling and an `Aspire.AppHost.Sdk` AppHost project.
    75	- Docker and [Dapr](https://docs.dapr.io) initialized locally (`dapr init`).
    76	
    77	## Notes
    78	
    79	- Dev pub/sub is backed by Redis on a fixed host port (6380; `dapr init` owns 6379), and contract-backed mocks by Microcks
    80	  on 8585; the generated YAML points at them. This resolves the generate-before-run ordering; a port
    81	  conflict there is a known limitation.
    82	- Synchronous APIs (`Provides`/`Consumes`) create no Dapr component — Dapr service invocation
    83	  addresses providers by app-id, which the sidecars already establish. A `MockApi` declaration is
    84	  the exception: it emits an `HTTPEndpoint` resource named after the (skipped) provider.
    85	- Topic mocking is out of scope, for protocol reasons among others: Microcks' async minion
    86	  does not speak Redis (ADR 0006, amended again).
    87	- The runtime-config contract injected into each project (`INTROPY__COMPONENT`, `INTROPY__CONFIG`)
    88	  is provisional until the Intropy Hosting framework consumes it.
